Records each individual partial matching between debit and credit journal items (account.move.line), allowing progressive reconciliation while keeping track of residual amounts.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Partial payments on invoices/bills (e.g. 60% paid, 40% remaining)
Partial bank reconciliation (matching part of a statement line)
Handling over-payments, advances, and credit notes applied partially
Multi-currency partial matching with exchange differences
Basis for computing amount_residual on every move line
Foundation for full reconciliation (account.full.reconcile)

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent, lightweight)
Key Fields:
debit_move_id, credit_move_id → account.move.line
amount, debit_amount_currency, credit_amount_currency
currency_id, company_currency_id, company_id
full_reconcile_id → account.full.reconcile (when completed)
exchange_move_id (for forex difference)
max_date (for aging reports)

Critical Hooks: create, unlink (cascades residual recalculation), _check_full_reconcile
No state field — existence = active partial reconciliation
Security: Controlled through move line access rights

RAG Routing Keywords:
partial reconcile, partial reconciliation, partial payment, residual amount, amount residual, unmatched portion, partial matching, partial bank recon, remaining balance, open amount, unreconciled portion, partial application
Related Models (most joined):

account.move.line (debit_move_id & credit_move_id)
account.full.reconcile (parent when fully reconciled)
account.move
account.bank.statement.line
account.payment

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.partial.reconcile is the Odoo model that stores every partial matching between two account.move.line records (debit and credit) with reconciled amount, currency amounts, and links to full_reconcile_id when completed. It powers residual amount calculation, partial payments, progressive bank reconciliation, multi-currency handling, and forms the core of Odoo’s reconciliation engine together with account.full.reconcile.